{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything the default placeholders — and your own custom ones — get for free: VoiceOver, Reduce Motion, Increase Contrast, Dynamic Type, and stable identifiers for XCUITest."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Accessibility"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/accessibility"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"title":"Accessibility","roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A placeholder is often the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"only"}]},{"type":"text","text":" thing on screen for a few hundred milliseconds, or the only thing a user with a slow connection sees for much longer than that — so it’s worth it being as accessible as the real content it stands in for. The default "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateDefault{Empty,Loading,Error}View"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIView"},{"type":"text","text":"s handle all of this out of the box; this article rounds up what they do and how a fully custom placeholder can match them."}]},{"anchor":"VoiceOver-announcements","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"VoiceOver announcements"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each default placeholder announces its own appearance — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AccessibilityNotification.Announcement(_:).post()"},{"type":"text","text":" in SwiftUI, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIAccessibility.post(notification:.announcement, argument:)"},{"type":"text","text":" in UIKit — so a screen settling into "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".empty"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".loading"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".error"},{"type":"text","text":" is heard, not just seen."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/accessibilityAnnouncement"},{"type":"text","text":" exposes that same wording for any case, so a fully custom placeholder can announce transitions consistently instead of inventing its own text:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":[".onAppear {","    if let announcement = state.accessibilityAnnouncement {","        AccessibilityNotification.Announcement(announcement).post()","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":" — your own content is what VoiceOver should read at that point — and, for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".empty"},{"type":"text","text":", it’s the default “Nothing Here” text; announce your own custom title directly instead if your placeholder shows one, so VoiceOver matches what’s on screen. See "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit"},{"type":"text","text":" for the full examples."}]},{"anchor":"Reduce-Motion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Reduce Motion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default Loading placeholder’s ring spins via a repeating rotation animation — purely decorative, and exactly the kind of large, continuous motion Reduce Motion exists to suppress. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateDefaultLoadingView"},{"type":"text","text":" reads SwiftUI’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"accessibilityReduceMotion"},{"type":"text","text":" environment value; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateDefaultLoadingUIView"},{"type":"text","text":" reads "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIAccessibility.isReduceMotionEnabled"},{"type":"text","text":" and also observes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIAccessibility.reduceMotionStatusDidChangeNotification"},{"type":"text","text":", so an already-visible spinner responds immediately if the setting changes while on screen, not just on the next appearance. Either way, the ring stays static — still colorful, just not spinning — instead of disabling itself entirely, since a static ring still communicates “loading” on its own."}]},{"anchor":"Increase-Contrast","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Increase Contrast"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All three default placeholders’ gradient icons\/ring respect Increase Contrast — SwiftUI’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"colorSchemeContrast"},{"type":"text","text":" environment value, UIKit’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIAccessibility.isDarkerSystemColorsEnabled"},{"type":"text","text":" (observed live the same way Reduce Motion is). A multi-stop gradient can dip below an acceptable contrast ratio in places a single flat color never does, so when Increase Contrast is on, every gradient is swapped for a solid "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".label"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".primary"},{"type":"text","text":" tint instead."}]},{"anchor":"Dynamic-Type","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Dynamic Type"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default Empty\/Error placeholders’ text scales with Dynamic Type: SwiftUI’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ErrorView"},{"type":"text","text":" get this for free from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ContentUnavailableView"},{"type":"text","text":"’s own text styles, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateDefaultEmptyUIView"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ErrorUIView"},{"type":"text","text":"’s labels use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIFont.preferredFont(forTextStyle: .body, compatibleWith:)"},{"type":"text","text":". Both are covered up to the largest accessibility size by snapshot tests, so a regression that silently pins the text to a fixed size would be caught. The default Loading placeholder has no text at all — its ring is a fixed-size shape, unaffected by Dynamic Type by design."}]},{"anchor":"Identifiers-for-XCUITest","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Identifiers for XCUITest"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every default placeholder exposes a stable "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"accessibilityIdentifier"},{"type":"text","text":", independent of any localized or custom text, so a UI test can assert which state is showing without string-matching:"}]},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Identifier"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Shown on"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screenStates.loading"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultLoadingView"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultLoadingUIView"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screenStates.empty"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultEmptyUIView"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screenStates.error"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultErrorView"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultErrorUIView"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"screenStates.error.retryButton","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Retry button, when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onRetry"},{"type":"text","text":" is given"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"screenStates.error.secondaryActionButton","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The secondary action button, when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"secondaryAction"},{"type":"text","text":" is given"}]}]]]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit"],"title":"Related Documentation"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"references":{"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Give any screen a standard "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Empty"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Loading"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Error"},{"type":"text","text":" state, usable from both UIKit and SwiftUI."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates","type":"topic","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"ScreenStates"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateDefaultLoadingView":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Default placeholder shown while a screen’s data is loading."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultLoadingView","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatedefaultloadingview","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScreenStateDefaultLoadingView","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScreenStateDefaultLoadingView","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"ScreenStateDefaultLoadingView"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateDefaultErrorUIView":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Default placeholder shown when a screen’s data failed to load, with an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"optional Retry button."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatedefaulterroruiview","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScreenStateDefaultErrorUIView","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ScreenStateDefaultErrorUIView","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultErrorUIView","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScreenStateDefaultErrorUIView","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateDefaultErrorView":{"abstract":[{"text":"Default placeholder shown when a screen’s data failed to load, with an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"optional retry action.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/